# Test authoring

Human contract: `docs/current/test-authoring.md`.
Domain grids: `tools/gametest_grids.json`.
Checker: `tools/check_gametest_hygiene.py`.

## Pick the layer

- Pure logic / data / JSON / counts → JUnit.
- Only real-world placement, capabilities, ticking → GameTest.
- Do not iterate hundreds of thousands of recipes inside a GameTest.

## Fixtures

- Use `GameTestFixtures.requireMaterialStack` and `requirePipe`.
- Use only parts GT6 registers and CC already registers. Check
  `gt6_code/gregtech6` and `python tools/gt6_resolve.py` first.
- No pure tin or iron pipes (GT6 has none). Non-gasproof pipe → wood /
  treated wood fluid pipe.
- Missing part = assertion failure. Never swap in another material, prefix,
  or vanilla item.
- Copy the material `ItemStack`; `new ItemStack(item)` drops components.
- A test that intentionally rejects a missing part needs a previous-line
  `hygiene-negative:` comment.

## Expected values

- GT6 source fact (blade count, energy side): may be literal; cite
  `gt6-source:` on the same or previous line.
- Projection of our own data (recipe / EMI / catalog counts): compare against
  runtime catalog or generated manifest. New 3-digit assertion literals fail
  the hygiene ratchet. VD-2026-09-003 stays open for the existing ones.
- Performance: separate budget assert. Never raise budget constants to go green.
- Changing a literal: state which data change caused it.

## GameTest must not throw

```java
// BAD
var be = (FooBlockEntity) helper.getBlockEntity(pos);
var r = map.findMatch(q).orElseThrow();
// GOOD
var be = GameTestRequirements.requireBlockEntity(helper, pos, FooBlockEntity.class);
var r = GameTestRequirements.requirePresent(optional, "no match for " + q);
```

- `level.getCapability` needs `helper.absolutePos(pos)`, or
  `GameTestRequirements.requireCapability`.
- `GameTestFailures.fail` truncates to 900 characters.
- Place machines with `GameTestMachinePlacement`. Electrolyzer and centrifuge
  take power from the bottom.

## Running

- `.\gradlew.bat runGameTestServer -PgameTestGrid=<id>`.
- `-PgameTestFilter` is diagnosis only; close on the grid.
- `-PwaveRecipes` is only an in-progress namespace. Committed holders must not
  keep `cruciblecraft_wave_`.
- Never treat `gametest_receipt.json` as PASS.
- Never delete tests, drop `required`, or skip failures.
- A failure that stays needs an entry in
  `tools/waves/prep/test-authoring-workflow/disposition.json`.
